================================================================================
Bundled snippets
================================================================================

Most snippet files under src/main/resources/com/editora/snippets/ (the
VS Code-format *.json files for C, C++, C#, CSS, Go, HTML, Java, Kotlin,
Markdown, PowerShell, Python, Ruby, Rust, shell, and SQL) are taken from the
"friendly-snippets" collection and redistributed under the MIT License:

    friendly-snippets — https://github.com/rafamadriz/friendly-snippets
    Copyright (c) 2021 Rafael Madriz
    License: MIT

The core language files are vendored unmodified (framework-specific extras are
not included), except python.json: its shebang names python3, the class
template uses no Python 2 super() call, and the try/except snippets re-raise
with a bare raise; and java.json, which started from friendly-snippets and was
largely rewritten for Editora: fixed bodies (class name, package, semicolons),
arrow switch, records, sealed types, streams, text blocks, virtual threads,
JUnit 5, and IntelliJ-style alias triggers. The remaining snippet files (xml,
batchfile, groovy, scala, clojure, json, yaml, ini, global) are original to
Editora and covered by Editora's own MIT License.

